//? Title: Global Pooling versus Flattening: What the Head Forgets
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A classifier head must summarise a spatial feature map. Global average pooling shares
evidence across locations but discards spatial arrangement, while flattening retains location
with more parameters. We check the exact invariance and gradient identities, then train both
heads on controlled appearance and location tasks.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/global_pooling_vs_flatten.cpp`.

> The method

For a feature map F of shape [N,H,W,C] and K classes, GAP followed by a dense head learns
CK+K scalars. A flatten-linear head learns HWCK+K. The GAP logit and its derivative are

$$
z_k=b_k+\frac1{HW}\sum_{h,w,c}F_{h,w,c}W_{c,k},\qquad
\frac{\partial z_k}{\partial F_{h,w,c}}=\frac{W_{c,k}}{HW}.
$$
\alttext(A GAP logit is the spatial average of its class activation map, and every spatial position receives the same per-channel derivative.)

Permuting spatial sites leaves GAP logits unchanged. This follows by reindexing a finite
sum, and it applies to the feature map: padding or strided feature extraction can break
image-level shift equivariance. The class-activation map is sum_c F_hwc W_ck, whose average
plus bias recovers the logit. Flattening can distinguish left from right; GAP cannot when
those maps have identical channel averages. A forward head costs O(HWC+CK) for GAP or
O(HWCK) for flattening. The controlled tasks isolate heads, not jointly trained CNNs.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.tikz > build/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.svg build/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.dvi > build/global_pooling_vs_flatten_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
